npm/android-fix.mjs
*.tgz
npm/
phone-use/dsh-plugin-phone-use/

# Scratch images (screenshots pasted into a session, throwaway renders). The repo
# publishes no images of its own, so a bare *.jpg/*.jpeg/*.webp here would only
# ever catch loose files that were never meant to be committed.
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.webp

# android-app: build outputs, the 27 MB Android platform stub, and the signing key are all
# machine-local. The key is deliberately NOT published: anyone holding it could sign an APK that
# installs as an update over this one. A fresh clone simply generates its own key on first build,
# which only costs the ability to update over an existing install (uninstall + reinstall instead).
android-app/out/
android-app/tools/android.jar
android-app/tools/icon-preview.png
android-app/keystore.jks
